file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh owner_lap_read and owner_lap_detail beside owner_transcript, called from both refusals; a detached pass reads lap=detached and is given launch_head against HEAD
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh nineteen readings on the plant --detach actually makes, including the elder parent reading still firing and the same plant against a detection-disabled copy
file tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish nineteen assertions, two of them asserting the defect rather than the repair
file construction/archive/REDS-the-loom-that-chased-a-generation-too-far-rows-681.md row %681 booked and folded in one lap, the pin having 1,509 bytes against a row of three thousand
file construction/ITINERARY.md COPAL block replaced; elder shelved whole with its trailing line repaired
scope one keystone -- the liveness reading, its two callers, its control and witness, and the ledger row
status GREEN -- cold open 196 green 0 red tree_moved=no; standing_equipment green 100s with the witness's nineteen new assertions; the REDS, log-index and roster families green on the committed tree. Three reds met and cleared: a 679/680 gap and an unresolved upstream index row, both cured by the rebase, and instrument_refusal from a peer's commit, named rather than rewritten and closed by their own next one.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- lap=detached says ancestry cannot answer, so a detached pass whose lap truly died reads like a live one whenever the tree has NOT moved. Naming the launcher inside the lock is the next generation and it is a fleet decision, not a lap.
